Reason: the draw list is rebuilt whenever an instance is created or destroyed, which in a fight is most frames. Each
rebuild pulled the room's tiles back out of the old list, re-read every tile's depth and checked their order, then
merged the instances in by comparing them with every tile. In rm_a3h04 (4,787 tiles) that cost about 3.9 ms a rebuild
on the real Wii, 3 ms of it tile work, while sand crumbling rebuilt the list on a quarter of all frames. The sorted
tile run is now kept between rebuilds while the room, its tile array, its tile count and a tile-order version (moved
by every tile builtin that changes a depth or which tiles there are, and by every room change) all hold; and each
instance finds its place among the tiles by binary search, with the same comparisons, so the order is the same.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

